{"uid":"21f7d1a5671a6b61","name":"test_script_filters_the_docker_tier_out_when_a_usable_socket_is_present","fullName":"tests.test_host_like_pytest_script#test_script_filters_the_docker_tier_out_when_a_usable_socket_is_present","historyId":"a77c72fd42c300a938504bb666c39876","time":{"start":1791915527111,"stop":1791915528518,"duration":1407},"description":"F2 (#74): rather than let the docker-marked modules attempt to run\n    nested (and time out against a bridge-gateway port this container\n    cannot reach), the script must detect a usable docker socket and\n    exclude the tier with ``-m \"not docker\"`` -- proven here by collecting\n    a real docker-marked module through the script and asserting nothing\n    from it is collected.\n\n    Made hermetic (#109): this must hold regardless of whether *this*\n    container happens to have a real docker socket mounted in, so it\n    fabricates its own usable-socket precondition instead of relying on\n    the ambient environment -- a fake ``docker`` executable on ``PATH``\n    that exits 0 for ``docker version`` (matching the script's own probe,\n    ``command -v docker`` + ``-S \"${DOCKER_SOCK_PATH:-/var/run/docker.sock}\"``\n    + a ``docker version`` round-trip), plus a real bound unix socket at a\n    path handed to the script via ``DOCKER_SOCK_PATH`` so the ``-S`` test\n    passes without touching ``/var/run/docker.sock``.","descriptionHtml":"<p>F2 (#74): rather than let the docker-marked modules attempt to run<br />\nnested (and time out against a bridge-gateway port this container<br />\ncannot reach), the script must detect a usable docker socket and<br />\nexclude the tier with <code>-m &quot;not docker&quot;</code> -- proven here by collecting<br />\na real docker-marked module through the script and asserting nothing<br />\nfrom it is collected.</p>\n<pre><code>Made hermetic (#109): this must hold regardless of whether *this*\ncontainer happens to have a real docker socket mounted in, so it\nfabricates its own usable-socket precondition instead of relying on\nthe ambient environment -- a fake ``docker`` executable on ``PATH``\nthat exits 0 for ``docker version`` (matching the script's own probe,\n``command -v docker`` + ``-S &quot;${DOCKER_SOCK_PATH:-/var/run/docker.sock}&quot;``\n+ a ``docker version`` round-trip), plus a real bound unix socket at a\npath handed to the script via ``DOCKER_SOCK_PATH`` so the ``-S`` test\npasses without touching ``/var/run/docker.sock``.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791915518558,"stop":1791915518558,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791915518559,"stop":1791915518559,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791915527102,"stop":1791915527103,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791915527103,"stop":1791915527105,"duration":2},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791915527105,"stop":1791915527106,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_en